 "disclaimers": {
  "product": "**NOT A RECOMMENDATION. The v1 model has no demonstrated edge.** It failed its signed 2025-26 confirmation test. Closing-line value on spreads was +0.35 points against the pre-registered +0.5 bar (permutation p = 0.0006: a real but small effect), and on totals +0.03 points (p = 0.25). Settled against the closing line, its spread picks won 49.5% and its totals picks 49.4%. Its average error was 11.5 points against the market close's 10.9. This page only shows the model next to the market. Early in the season its ratings are almost entirely last season's, and it does not use injuries. The market line is the median across books, which can fall between two numbers nobody offers. For games where The Odds API had no line, the market line is ESPN's own current line, usually from one book, and n_books says how many.",
  "totals": "**TOTALS: NOT A RECOMMENDATION.** The totals model's closing-line value in the signed confirmation was +0.03 points (95% interval -0.21 to +0.25, p = 0.25), which is not distinguishable from zero. The pattern seen in discovery did not replicate. **There is no demonstrated totals edge.**"
